# ZedProxy dependency-audit allowlist
# =============================================================================
# Temporary, justified exceptions to the vulnerability-audit policy enforced by
# install.sh / update.sh / CI (see scripts/lib/supply-chain-lib.sh).
#
# Policy recap:
#   critical  → always fails the install/CI (NEVER allowlistable)
#   high      → fails UNLESS an UNEXPIRED entry below covers it
#   moderate/low → reported, not blocking
#
# One entry per line, pipe-separated, with EXACTLY five fields:
#
#   package|advisory|reason|expiry(YYYY-MM-DD)|owner
#
#   package  — exact composer/npm package name (e.g. guzzlehttp/guzzle)
#   advisory — advisory id / CVE / URL reported by the auditor
#   reason   — why the risk is temporarily accepted (no blank/fake entries)
#   expiry   — ISO date; the entry is IGNORED on or after this date
#   owner    — who accepted the risk and will remove the entry
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored. An entry with a missing
# or malformed expiry date is treated as EXPIRED (i.e. it does NOT suppress the
# finding). Do not add blanket or wildcard entries — each must name one package
# and one advisory.
#
# Example (commented out — not active):
# example/package|CVE-2099-0001|Upstream fix pending release; no exploit path in our usage|2099-01-01|security@zedproxy
